---
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
import ProjectTags from "../../components/ProjectTags.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout>
  {/* HERO */}
  <section class="mb-12">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">
          Robotic Arm for Automated Fiber Placement
        </h1>

        <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 max-w-3xl">
          I simulated automated fiber placement with a UR5e in PyDrake. A roller end-effector follows a surface trajectory using operational-space impedance control to regulate contact forces and recover from disturbances.
        </p>

        <ProjectTags />
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg shadow-md overflow-hidden w-full">
        <video
          class="w-full h-auto"
          autoplay
          controls
          muted
          loop
          playsinline
          preload="metadata"
          poster="/media/afp/example.jpg"
        >
          <source src="/media/afp/hero.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          <img
            src="/media/afp/example.jpg"
            alt="Industrial automated fiber placement system example"
            class="w-full h-auto"
          />
        </video>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* AT A GLANCE */}
  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">At a Glance</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
      <div class="rounded-lg border bg-white p-4 shadow-sm">
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">Robot + Sim</div>
        <div class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-800">UR5e + PyDrake</div>
        <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Hydroelastic contact</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border bg-white p-4 shadow-sm">
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">Control</div>
        <div class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-800">Operational impedance</div>
        <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Inverse dynamics tracking</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border bg-white p-4 shadow-sm">
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">Objective</div>
        <div class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-800">Stable contact</div>
        <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Bounded force + recovery</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border bg-white p-4 shadow-sm">
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">Validation</div>
        <div class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-800">Push test + path pass</div>
        <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Single-pass + full run</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* OVERVIEW */}
  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Overview</h2>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-start">
      <div class="text-gray-700 space-y-4">
        <p class="text-gray-600">
          AFP lays composite tow along a prescribed path while a roller compacts material against a mold. The control challenge is maintaining consistent normal force and alignment while following a surface path under compliance, geometry mismatch, and disturbances.
        </p>

        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
          <li><span class="font-medium">Robot:</span> UR5e in Drake's multibody simulation</li>
          <li><span class="font-medium">End effector:</span> roller modeled as a rigid body attached to the wrist</li>
          <li><span class="font-medium">Environment:</span> compliant mold surface as contact geometry</li>
          <li><span class="font-medium">Control goal:</span> stable force interaction + trajectory tracking via impedance control</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-6">
        <img
          src="/media/afp/example.jpg"
          alt="AFP example showing robot and layup concept"
          class="rounded-lg shadow-sm w-full"
        />
        <img
          src="/media/afp/roller-schematic.png"
          alt="AFP head schematic showing roller and material placement"
          class="rounded-lg shadow-sm w-full"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* TRAJECTORY GENERATION */}
  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Trajectory Generation</h2>

    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div class="text-gray-700 space-y-4">
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
          <li>Represent mold surface (Bezier surface or mesh)</li>
          <li>Generate reference curve via surface intersection or parametric sampling</li>
          <li>Compute desired pose along the curve — position + surface-consistent orientation</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="text-gray-600">
          For planar molds, the path is generated by intersecting a plane with the surface and sampling along the result. For curved molds, the same approach extends parametrically. The output is a time-parameterized end-effector pose reference for the controller.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <figure class="rounded-lg shadow-sm overflow-hidden bg-white border">
          <img
            src="/media/afp/trajectory-planar.png"
            alt="Planar trajectory generation visualization"
            class="w-full h-auto"
          />
          <figcaption class="px-3 py-2 text-sm text-gray-600">Planar trajectory</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="rounded-lg shadow-sm overflow-hidden bg-white border">
          <img
            src="/media/afp/trajectory-mesh.png"
            alt="Curved mold mesh generation visualization"
            class="w-full h-auto"
          />
          <figcaption class="px-3 py-2 text-sm text-gray-600">Curved mold mesh</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* CONTROLLER DESIGN */}
  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Controller Design</h2>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-start">
      <div class="text-gray-700 space-y-4">
        <p class="text-gray-600">
          The controller uses a virtual mass-spring-damper relationship between actual end-effector motion and the desired trajectory. This gives the roller compliance when surface variation or an external push displaces it from the reference path.
        </p>

        <div class="rounded-md border bg-gray-50 p-4 text-sm text-gray-700 overflow-auto">
          <div class="font-semibold mb-2">Impedance model</div>
          <div>
            F = M (ẍ − ẍ<sub>d</sub>) + B (ẋ − ẋ<sub>d</sub>) + K (x − x<sub>d</sub>)
          </div>
          <div class="mt-2 text-gray-600">
            where x is the end-effector position and x<sub>d</sub> is the desired trajectory.
          </div>
        </div>

        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
          <li><span class="font-medium">Output:</span> desired task-space accelerations → inverse dynamics torques</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-6">
        <img
          src="/media/afp/impedance-block-diagram.png"
          alt="Impedance control block diagram"
          class="rounded-lg shadow-sm w-full"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* RESULTS */}
  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Results</h2>

    <div class="space-y-8">
      <div class="text-gray-700 space-y-4">
        <p class="text-gray-600">
          I tested disturbance recovery with an external push and tracking along a generated surface pass. The tuned single pass maintained bounded pose error and contact forces. Longer runs showed force spikes at some transitions.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-semibold">Key outcomes</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
          <li><span class="font-medium">Damped disturbance rejection:</span> push test produced smooth recovery without runaway contact forces.</li>
          <li><span class="font-medium">Tracking (single pass):</span> end-effector pose error stayed tightly bounded during the tuned pass.</li>
          <li><span class="font-medium">Force regulation:</span> normal-force behavior remained controlled during nominal rolling.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="font-semibold mt-6">Limitations</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
          <li><span class="font-medium">Planar assumptions:</span> orientation targets were simplified; a curved mold requires surface-normal alignment and nonzero desired angular rates.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        <figure class="rounded-lg shadow-sm overflow-hidden bg-white border">
          <img
            src="/media/afp/push-test-force-plot.png"
            alt="End-effector force response (single pass)"
            class="w-full h-auto"
          />
          <figcaption class="px-3 py-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
            Force (single pass)
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <figure class="rounded-lg shadow-sm overflow-hidden bg-white border">
          <img
            src="/media/afp/ee-spatial-error-singlepass.png"
            alt="End-effector spatial error (single pass)"
            class="w-full h-auto"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption class="px-3 py-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
            Spatial error (single pass)
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <figure class="rounded-lg shadow-sm overflow-hidden bg-white border">
          <img
            src="/media/afp/ee-orientation-error-singlepass.png"
            alt="End-effector orientation error (single pass)"
            class="w-full h-auto"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption class="px-3 py-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
            Orientation error (single pass)
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <details class="rounded-lg border bg-white p-4 shadow-sm">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-gray-800">Show full-trajectory plots</summary>
        <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-3 gap-4">
          <figure class="rounded-lg shadow-sm overflow-hidden bg-white border">
            <img
              src="/media/afp/push-test-force-plot_2.png"
              alt="End-effector force (full trajectory)"
              class="w-full h-auto"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <figcaption class="px-3 py-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
              Force (full trajectory)
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="rounded-lg shadow-sm overflow-hidden bg-white border">
            <img
              src="/media/afp/ee-spatial-error-fulltraj.png"
              alt="End-effector spatial error (full trajectory)"
              class="w-full h-auto"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <figcaption class="px-3 py-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
              Spatial error (full trajectory)
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="rounded-lg shadow-sm overflow-hidden bg-white border">
            <img
              src="/media/afp/ee-orientation-error-fulltraj.png"
              alt="End-effector orientation error (full trajectory)"
              class="w-full h-auto"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <figcaption class="px-3 py-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
              Orientation error (full trajectory)
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* LESSONS + NEXT STEPS */}
  <section class="mb-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Lessons & Next Steps</h2>

    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-3 text-gray-600">
      <li><span class="font-medium">Gain scheduling across phases:</span> retune or schedule gains for approach → contact → roll → lift to reduce transition spikes.</li>
      <li><span class="font-medium">Curved molds:</span> generate desired pose from surface normals and add nonzero desired angular rates for stable alignment.</li>
      <li><span class="font-medium">Model realism:</span> add sensor noise, filtering delay, and friction variability to stress-test the controller.</li>
      <li><span class="font-medium">Compare controllers:</span> benchmark against hybrid force–motion control to quantify tradeoffs.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</ProjectLayout>
